Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:22:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/32] Finish the guarded Manager workflow for trusted capture
 sessions

The completed flow replaces broker and private-reader paths with a validated draft, direct Framework transaction, compact Material 3 UI, owner authentication, recovery, actionable validation, and bilingual lifecycle-safe state.

Constraint: Final acceptance is the lemonadep userdebug target; source expansion uses -j2 and compilation uses -j8.
Rejected: Generic property editor and persistent warning banners | they weaken authority boundaries and obscure actionable state.
Confidence: high
Scope-risk: broad
Directive: Treat STATUS.md as the Manager completion boundary; reopen architecture only for a new contract or regression.
Tested: R0dumpManager and R0dumpManagerTests build; 44/44 instrumentation tests; source contracts; physical UI checks; live transaction/recovery matrix; final generation 262 enabled 0 under SELinux Enforcing.
Not-tested: Generated artifacts are intentionally excluded from git; FrameworksCoreTests has an unrelated external compile blocker.
