+# R0dump Manager Product
+
+## Register
+
+product
+
+## Users
+
+ROM developers and trusted device operators configuring r0dump capture sessions on an Android 16 owner-user device. Their recurring workflow is to select a target, choose capture points, validate limits, publish, launch, inspect, and end the session.
+
+## Product Purpose
+
+Provide a guarded system UI for the allowlisted `persist.sys.r0dump.fusion.*` contract. Success means the device state is always legible, drafts cannot be mistaken for published values, dangerous operations require device authentication, and every mutation is verified by read-back.
+
+## Brand Personality
+
+Precise, restrained, trustworthy. The interface should feel like an Android system tool, not a debugging demo or a marketing surface.
+
+## Anti-references
+
+- Arbitrary property editors that expose unrestricted `setprop` access.
+- Card-heavy dashboards, oversized status heroes, decorative motion, gradients, or glass effects.
+- Dense engineering consoles that require users to memorize bit numbers, byte limits, or generation rules.
+- Custom controls that replace familiar Android and Material 3 affordances.
+
+## Design Principles
+
+1. Put authoritative device state before editable content.
+2. Keep draft state visibly separate from the published snapshot.
+3. Make the common capture workflow fast and progressively disclose dangerous controls.
+4. Treat authentication, validation, and read-back as part of every mutation.
+5. Prefer familiar Android controls and compact, scannable information hierarchy.
+
+## Accessibility & Inclusion
+
+Meet at least 4.5:1 contrast for body text, preserve 48 dp touch targets, expose meaningful descriptions for icon-only controls, support English and Simplified Chinese without truncation, follow system high-contrast and dark themes, and respect reduced-motion settings.
+
+The normative product and security contract remains [IMPLEMENTATION.md](IMPLEMENTATION.md).
