+# R0dump Manager Status
+
+## Current state
+
+**Completed and accepted on 2026-08-30.**
+
+This completion marker covers the Manager application, its narrow Framework publication entry, dedicated SELinux contract, product packaging, and the userdebug deployment and transaction workflow. ART capture quality, unpacking experiments, and later runtime data-plane work remain separate project tracks.
+
+## Acceptance evidence
+
+- Target: `lineage_lemonadep-bp4a-userdebug` on Android 16.
+- Build policy: source expansion with `-j2`; actual compilation with `-j8`.
+- Targeted Manager, Framework, and SELinux production artifacts built successfully.
+- Manager instrumentation: **44/44 tests passed** after the final UI, validation, Toast, and managed run-ID changes.
+- Manager source contracts passed for 34 Framework fields, 42 capture points, direct Framework transactions, product/SELinux packaging, Android 16 lifecycle behavior, and English/Simplified Chinese parity.
+- Physical-device checks passed for the budget reset icon, removed notification banner, ANR-protection ordering, one-shot draft Toast, actionable validation details, and automatic run-ID handling.
+- Live publication/recovery transaction matrix passed with read-back verification.
+- Final device state: generation `262`, enabled `0`, SELinux `Enforcing`, no active target process.
+
+## Completion boundary
+
+- No additional `user` build is required for Manager acceptance.
+- Framework core production code built successfully. The broader `FrameworksCoreTests` target still has unrelated pre-existing lock-screen test compile errors; this is not a Manager acceptance blocker.
+- Further work should not reopen Manager architecture or UX unless a new regression, requirement, or runtime contract change is identified.
